"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[7984],{81461:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"Creates a Crown Grab round and immediately crowns every other player in the\\nround list, so the field starts split between holders and hunters.\\n\\nAlso watches for leavers so a departed player does not keep a phantom crown in\\n`crownHolders` and hold the round open.\\n\\nHandout happens here rather than in an `Init` hook, which means it runs before\\n[BaseGameMode:Start] has spawned anyone \u2014 players without a living character at\\nconstruction time are silently skipped by [CrownGrab:GiveCrown].","params":[{"name":"props","desc":"","lua_type":"MinigameTypes.GameModeProps"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"CrownGrab"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":123,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameModes/CrownGrab.luau"}},{"name":"GiveCrown","desc":"Crowns a player: attaches the crown accessory, slows them to\\n`HOLDER_WALK_SPEED`, and records them in `crownHolders`.\\n\\nRefuses when the player is dead, has no character, or is already wearing a\\ncrown \u2014 the last check is what keeps a hunter from accumulating crowns.\\n\\nThe steal handler on the crown\'s handle is armed 0.4s later, so the player you\\njust took it from cannot instantly take it back. When it fires, the old wearer\\nis un-crowned and their speed restored, the crown instance is destroyed, and\\nthis method recurses to crown the thief with a fresh one.\\n\\nA death listener removes the crown from `crownHolders` if the wearer dies,\\nwhich permanently removes that crown from the round.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"Who to crown","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":169,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameModes/CrownGrab.luau"}},{"name":"Play","desc":"The round. Called by [BaseGameMode:Start] and yields until the countdown ends.\\n\\nAfter a two-second grace period it runs [BaseGameMode:GameCountdown] with a\\nper-second condition that keeps the round alive only while at least one crown\\nexists \u2014 so a round where every holder dies ends immediately rather than\\nrunning out the clock with nothing to contest.\\n\\nWhoever is still crowned when it ends is declared a winner. Multiple winners\\nare normal.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":236,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameModes/CrownGrab.luau"}},{"name":"Stop","desc":"Cleans up this mode\'s own connections.\\n\\n:::danger\\nThis **overrides** [BaseGameMode:Stop] without calling it. None of the base\\nteardown runs: winners are never paid, the round summary is never broadcast,\\n`playing` is never cleared, the map is never destroyed and characters are never\\nreloaded. Since [BaseGameMode:Start] finishes by calling `self:Stop()`, a Crown\\nGrab round ends by cleaning one Maid and leaving everything else live.\\n\\n`Stop` is not part of the subclass contract described on [BaseGameMode];\\nmode-specific teardown belongs on the `Stopping` or `Destroying` signals\\ninstead.\\n:::","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":266,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameModes/CrownGrab.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"CrownGrab","desc":"Round state, on top of everything inherited from [BaseGameMode].\\n\\n:::caution\\n`maid` **shadows** the round Maid that [BaseGameMode] allocates, since the\\nconstructor assigns to the same field after the base has already set it. The\\nbase class\'s own connections are consequently owned by a Maid nothing holds a\\nreference to, and are never cleaned up.\\n:::","fields":[{"name":"maid","lua_type":"Maid","desc":"Owns this mode\'s own connections, separate from the round Maid"},{"name":"crownHolders","lua_type":"{ [Player]: boolean }","desc":"Who is currently crowned"},{"name":"touched","lua_type":"{ [string]: boolean }","desc":"Unused"}],"source":{"line":97,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameModes/CrownGrab.luau"}}],"name":"CrownGrab","desc":"Keep-away minigame. Half the players start wearing a crown; anyone without one\\ncan steal a crown by touching its wearer. Whoever is wearing a crown when the\\ntimer runs out wins.\\n\\n### Rules\\n\\n- 2 players minimum, 120-second cap, rotates over `battle_islands`,\\n  `construction_site` and `volcano_beach`.\\n- Crowns are handed out at construction to every other player in the round\\n  list, so roughly half the field starts crowned and the rest start hunting.\\n- Wearing a crown slows you slightly (`Util.defaultWalkSpeed - 2`) \u2014 being\\n  crowned is a handicap, which is what keeps holders moving instead of camping.\\n- Touching a crown\'s handle transfers it: the wearer loses it and their speed\\n  is restored, the toucher gains it. A player already holding a crown cannot\\n  steal a second, so crowns can never be concentrated.\\n- Crowns are armed 0.4s after being granted, preventing an instant re-steal by\\n  whoever you just took it from.\\n- A crown holder dying destroys their crown outright \u2014 it is removed from the\\n  game rather than dropped. The round therefore ends early once the last crown\\n  is gone.\\n\\nThe crown instance name includes a per-server random suffix (`CROWN_NAME`), so\\nthe mode\'s \\"is this player crowned?\\" check cannot be spoofed by another system\\nnaming an accessory `Crown`.\\n\\n### BaseGameMode hooks\\n\\nImplements [BaseGameMode] `Play`, and also **overrides `Stop`** \u2014 see the\\ncaution on [CrownGrab:Stop]. Crown handout happens in the constructor rather\\nthan in `Init`.\\n\\n`Play` yields on [BaseGameMode:GameCountdown] with a per-second condition that\\nends the round as soon as no crowns remain, then declares every surviving crown\\nholder a winner.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].Minigames \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks\\nenable it deliberately.","tags":["dormant"],"realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":47,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameModes/CrownGrab.luau"}}')}}]);